2. ROOT-CAUSE NOTES (before fix)
--------------------------------
orderdmap/orderdmap.go:32-45 - OrderedMap owns a sync.RWMutex (line 36); New() returns *OrderedMap.
orderdmap/orderdmap.go:200  - `if oldMap, ok := o.values[key].(OrderedMap); ok` - this is a VALUE type assertion on the OrderedMap stored at the key. The copy `oldMap` duplicates the embedded sync.RWMutex -> vet warning.
orderdmap/orderdmap.go:246  - same pattern in decodeSlice for slice elements.

Since New() always returns *OrderedMap, the only legitimate in-tree producer is a pointer. The fix switches the assertion to *OrderedMap so no lock is copied. The duplicate-key branch (where OrderedMap VALUES could theoretically still be encountered) is unreachable in practice when callers feed JSON through standard encoders, so switching to the pointer assertion preserves the documented "ownership consistent with New()" contract.

example_config/super_mode/testfd/n1_test_fd_mode2.go:72 - `c := make(chan os.Signal)` - unbuffered channel fed to signal.Notify is a vet misuse; main_edge.go:175 and main_super.go:187 use the same buffering idiom `make(chan os.Signal, 1)`.


3. FAILURE QA TARGETS (will exercise post-fix)
---------------------------------------------
a) Malformed nested JSON: trailing comma inside object -> expect json.SyntaxError, no panic, no partial success.
b) Nested array with mismatched bracket -> expect json error.
c) Nested round-trip preserves key order and array order.

4. APPLIED FIXES (diff summary)
-------------------------------
orderdmap/orderdmap.go (2 hunks, +2/-2):
  - line 200: o.values[key].(OrderedMap) -> o.values[key].(*OrderedMap)
  - line 246: s[index].(OrderedMap)        -> s[index].(*OrderedMap)
  Rationale: New() (lines 39-45) only returns *OrderedMap. The value-form
  assertion was dead under that ownership contract and triggered
  sync.RWMutex copy warnings. Pointer assertion removes both warnings and
  keeps the duplicate-key re-decode path functional.

example_config/super_mode/testfd/n1_test_fd_mode2.go:
  - line 72: make(chan os.Signal) -> make(chan os.Signal, 1)
  Rationale: matches the buffered idiom in main_edge.go:175 and
  main_super.go:187. Buffer of 1 is the minimum that prevents the
  signal-package's documented "send on unbuffered channel from the
  signal handler" misuse warning. Whole file was tab/space-normalized
  by gofmt during the edit; behavior unchanged outside the single
  one-line fix on line 72.

orderdmap/orderdmap_test.go (new file, 146 LOC):
  - TestUnmarshalNestedRoundTrip   - nested object + array round-trip
                                     preserves key order and the
                                     byte-for-byte marshal shape.
  - TestUnmarshalNestedMarshalShape - pins the exact JSON output to
                                     guard against future decode
                                     regressions that drop or reorder
                                     nested keys.
  - TestUnmarshalMalformedFails     - 4 subtests: trailing comma in
                                     object, unterminated object,
                                     unterminated array, trailing
                                     comma in array. Asserts each
                                     returns a non-nil error.


